      {
        "text": "# Filter Bubble\n\nA **filter bubble** is a situation where algorithms mostly show you content that matches what you already like or agree with, and hide other viewpoints or topics, often without you noticing.\n\n**Example:** When a site keeps recommending similar videos, posts, or news stories based on your past behavior, you can end up in a bubble where you rarely see different ideas or types of content.",
